Winch is a server configuration tool. It describes the desired state
of your servers in declarative YAML and provides commands to manage
that state.

Examples:
  # check the project without contacting a host
  winch validate
  # show the changes of the pipeline site on the test inventory
  winch plan site --inventory test
  # make those changes after a question
  winch apply site --inventory test

Usage:
  winch <command> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  validate  check the project without contacting a host
  fmt       format the project files
  plan      show the changes and change nothing
  apply     show the changes, ask, then make them
  run       plan and apply one module step
  exec      run a shell command on hosts
  secret    manage secrets and the age key
  doc       show the reference

Run "winch <command> --help" for the arguments and flags of a command.

See: winch doc
